02:36:00.090 --> 02:36:02.490
to the Mets on an exciting World

02:36:02.490 --> 02:36:04.570
Series and of course our thanks

02:36:04.570 --> 02:36:06.530
as well to the Boston Red Sox.

02:37:37.420 --> 02:37:45.220
All right, we are in the victorious Mets clubhouse, even as we look at Wade Boggs on the Red Sox bench.

02:37:45.220 --> 02:37:49.220
Commissioner Eubaroff, the manager of the ball club, Davy Johnson, the general manager, Frank Cashin.

02:37:49.220 --> 02:37:52.080
And for the presentation of the trophy, Commissioner Eubaroff.

02:37:52.080 --> 02:37:58.080
Very quickly, I'm pleased to tell you that there's a wire from the President of the United States congratulating the Mets.

02:37:58.080 --> 02:38:00.000
He's watched all the games.

02:38:00.000 --> 02:38:03.240
happy congratulating you and he's invited the entire team everyone from

02:38:03.240 --> 02:38:06.840
the organization to the White House well that's very nice and we certainly will

02:38:06.840 --> 02:38:11.000
go and we appreciate that let me tell you it's very special very special for

02:38:11.000 --> 02:38:14.780
baseball and I'd like to present you right now and this in this great big guy

02:38:14.780 --> 02:38:22.570
I can his trophy Fred Wilpon looking for Fred Wilpon one of the owners of the

02:38:22.570 --> 02:38:30.000
ball club Davey it's a heavy one great I think I can hold it seven games

02:38:30.120 --> 02:38:33.880
you did it all the way congratulations it doesn't get any better than this peter this is what it's

02:38:33.880 --> 02:38:47.160
all about frank we'll start with you you were the architect of bringing this ball club along in a

02:38:47.160 --> 02:38:52.120
few years time from a last place team to a team that won 108 during the regular season and now

02:38:52.120 --> 02:38:56.740
reigns as world champions your thoughts well my thoughts are that we had great ownership

02:38:56.740 --> 02:39:00.000
mr will punt mr doubleday give us the time to really read

02:39:00.000 --> 02:39:05.040
rebuild this ball club, and people like Al Harrison and Joe McElvain and Steve Shriver

02:39:05.040 --> 02:39:09.000
and Harry Miner, plus Davey and some great ballplayers, we were able to do it.

02:39:09.060 --> 02:39:13.740
So always be appreciative of the ownership, and it's great to be a winner, as you know,

02:39:13.800 --> 02:39:17.580
and I thank the fans of New York and the people everywhere that supported us.

02:39:18.020 --> 02:39:19.260
Let's get a word here from Davey.

02:39:19.640 --> 02:39:24.620
Strange and unfair as it might seem, if one thing or another broke a different way Saturday

02:39:24.620 --> 02:39:28.420
night, you come up short, and some people, unfair as it would have been, would have said

02:39:28.420 --> 02:39:29.240
failure.

02:39:29.820 --> 02:39:30.000
Well,

02:39:30.000 --> 02:39:33.520
that's what this game's all about. You can never take anything for granted. Strange things happen.

02:39:33.620 --> 02:39:38.120
You just keep plugging away. And it happened for us. We deserve it. We had the best record in

02:39:38.120 --> 02:39:41.660
baseball. We should be the world champs. Your thoughts about the Boston Red Sox?

02:39:42.030 --> 02:39:46.120
They're a great ball club. You know, it was very touch and go. Both, you know, break here, break

02:39:46.120 --> 02:39:50.970
there, and they could have been world champs. But the good guys got it. Is there any way to describe

02:39:50.970 --> 02:39:54.910
the roller coaster? Two out, bottom of the 10th Saturday, and you're standing here now?

02:39:55.460 --> 02:39:59.130
Well, that's baseball. That's what makes it so beautiful. You know, it's never over till it's

02:39:59.130 --> 02:40:00.000
I think somebody said,

02:40:00.000 --> 02:40:04.880
that and this is what it's all about. This is what it's all worth sweating for.

02:40:04.880 --> 02:40:08.920
Davey, congratulations. Thank you, Bobby. A quick word from Fred Wilpon, one of the

02:40:08.920 --> 02:40:12.500
owners of the ball club. I'm very thrilled. I'm thrilled for New York. I'm thrilled for

02:40:12.500 --> 02:40:18.000
the New York Mets. Boston Red Sox have nothing to be ashamed of. They played great baseball,

02:40:18.000 --> 02:40:23.810
great character from both sides. Frank Cashin and his organization here is, I think, the

02:40:23.810 --> 02:40:30.000
best of baseball and I love him. I love it for New York. We're going to try and get Ray Knight up here.

02:40:30.990 --> 02:40:33.830
Before we speak with Ray Knight, the most valuable player,

02:40:33.830 --> 02:40:38.060
we're going to go to the other side, to the Boston Clubhouse and Marv Albert. Marv?

02:40:38.060 --> 02:40:42.100
All right, Bob, and this man to my right, Bruce Hurst of the Red Sox,

02:40:42.100 --> 02:40:46.000
who had a splendid World Series, winning two games, not able to do it tonight.

02:40:46.000 --> 02:40:51.100
But on Saturday night, at one point, you were actually voted most valuable player of the series

02:40:51.100 --> 02:40:55.480
before the game was over. I know this has to be a difficult moment for you.

02:40:55.480 --> 02:41:00.000
Well, you know, I'd rather trade all that stuff for the World Championship.

02:41:00.540 --> 02:41:05.280
We battled hard all year long, and we came back, and today we tried, but we just didn't

02:41:05.280 --> 02:41:06.880
have enough, and you have to tip your hat to the Mets.

02:41:08.000 --> 02:41:11.760
They came back, we beat them the first two, and they showed a lot of class and a lot of

02:41:11.760 --> 02:41:15.240
guts, and they have a lot of great players on their team, and you just have to give them

02:41:15.240 --> 02:41:15.480
credit.

02:41:16.080 --> 02:41:23.240
Bruce, of course, this is 1986, but ballplayers are very superstitious, and you look back

02:41:23.240 --> 02:41:30.000
to the Red Sox of 67, of 46, of 75, and people say they are snake-bitten. What is

02:41:30.350 --> 02:41:34.110
your reaction to that did that have any effect on this ballclub none whatsoever

02:41:34.110 --> 02:41:38.150
what happened in the past does have any bearing on what happened today we had

02:41:38.150 --> 02:41:42.170
every opportunity to win we had a chance to win on game six and we didn't put it

02:41:42.170 --> 02:41:45.800
away and we were in the game today and then we just let it slip away what

02:41:45.800 --> 02:41:49.200
happened in 46 and 75 and all those other years it doesn't make any

02:41:49.200 --> 02:41:52.060
difference it's a totally different ballclub different players whole

02:41:52.060 --> 02:41:55.480
different cast of characters and this team can win and we'll be back all right

02:41:55.480 --> 02:42:00.000
and we're told that Ray Knight won most valuable player award in the

02:42:00.000 --> 02:42:03.900
series and the last two games he's the man who did most of the damage he's a

02:42:03.900 --> 02:42:07.920
very good player I felt like all along for me to win he was one of the guys that

02:42:07.920 --> 02:42:10.860
I had to get out he's a great great hitter is a great two-strike hitter he

02:42:10.860 --> 02:42:13.840
doesn't strike out a lot and he's an outstanding player and I have to tip my

02:42:13.840 --> 02:42:17.580
hat to Ray he did a great job for them and then beat us all right Bruce thank

02:42:17.580 --> 02:42:22.200
you very much and Ray Knight the series MVP is alongside Bob Costas let's get

02:42:22.200 --> 02:42:27.120
back to the Met locker room Marv thank you and just a moment ago Ray Davy

02:42:27.120 --> 02:42:30.000
Johnson was saying it's just baseball it's the way it

02:42:30.000 --> 02:42:33.420
It is. You can go from goat to hero, from the bottom to the top.

02:42:33.480 --> 02:42:36.280
And it happened for you, certainly, in such graphic fashion.

02:42:36.560 --> 02:42:39.760
It surely did, man. I tell you, I was so down the other night after the era.

02:42:39.840 --> 02:42:41.560
But this is a game of redeeming features.

02:42:41.660 --> 02:42:45.340
And thank the good Lord I had a chance to come back, and we won that ballgame tonight.

02:42:45.680 --> 02:42:48.040
Just goes to show you, if you keep fighting in there, things can happen.

02:42:48.100 --> 02:42:49.300
And that's the way it's been for me all year.

02:42:49.590 --> 02:42:50.820
And just a great bunch of guys.

02:42:50.900 --> 02:42:52.790
And golly, I don't really know what to say.

02:42:52.830 --> 02:42:54.190
I'm just so excited and happy.

02:42:54.190 --> 02:42:55.830
And this is unbelievable.

02:42:56.390 --> 02:42:57.610
The home run that snapped the tie.

02:42:58.220 --> 02:42:59.510
Well, it was a fastball, 2-1.

02:42:59.670 --> 02:43:00.000
I was looking

02:43:00.000 --> 02:43:04.980
for a fastball tie ball game and I'm a fastball hitter and I just looked pitching up and kind

02:43:04.980 --> 02:43:08.280
of in the strike zone he threw it right there and I had a good swing at it I don't hit too

02:43:08.280 --> 02:43:13.990
many of them but I knew that was gone if he was up enough what did they say to you can

02:43:13.990 --> 02:43:17.150
you remember it all when you hit home plate and then the dugout well the last two nights

02:43:17.150 --> 02:43:21.230
I'm everything's been pretty numb for me my concentrations level's been so high they just

02:43:21.230 --> 02:43:24.800
hugged me and gave me high fives and all that and I don't really know what they said I was

02:43:24.800 --> 02:43:30.000
just uh emotionally spent again I've been exhausted the whole last couple of nights boy that's

02:43:31.300 --> 02:43:35.640
And just the feeling of when they touch your hand and all that stuff

02:43:35.640 --> 02:43:39.260
is such a feeling of togetherness and closeness.

02:43:39.680 --> 02:43:41.670
They really said a lot, but I don't remember what they said.

02:43:41.810 --> 02:43:43.310
Congratulations on being named MVP.

02:43:43.530 --> 02:43:44.170
Thank you very much.

02:43:44.210 --> 02:43:44.530
Unbelievable.

02:43:45.430 --> 02:43:47.230
Let's get Keith Hernandez in here.

02:43:49.360 --> 02:43:51.900
Keith, I was thinking as you came to bat in the sixth inning

02:43:51.900 --> 02:43:53.800
with the score 3-0 and the bases loaded.

02:43:54.140 --> 02:43:56.830
In 82 in the other World Series in which you played for the Cardinals,

02:43:57.250 --> 02:44:00.000
bottom of the sixth at Busch Stadium, trailing 3-1.

02:44:00.000 --> 02:44:02.260
bases loaded, left-handed pitcher on the mound.

02:44:02.260 --> 02:44:06.040
An almost unbelievably identical situation, and you also got a base hit there.

02:44:06.040 --> 02:44:07.930
Well, I remember that well.

02:44:07.930 --> 02:44:11.470
It tied the game, and it was two outs at the time.

02:44:11.470 --> 02:44:15.050
I fell, Bob, I swung the bat great the whole series, and everybody was saying, "Well, you're

02:44:15.050 --> 02:44:17.790
not hitting the ball," and I said, "Well, you can't look at the box scores."

02:44:17.790 --> 02:44:21.880
I've been hitting the ball good the whole series, and right at people, and I woke up

02:44:21.880 --> 02:44:22.880
this morning.

02:44:22.880 --> 02:44:27.450
I told my brother who was with me from California, Gary, I said, "If I get a chance with men

02:44:27.450 --> 02:44:29.320
on base today, I'm going to be the man."

02:44:30.000 --> 02:44:35.410
it just worked out great that way. At a bat, I was so confident and relaxed. I was just

02:44:35.410 --> 02:44:40.070
up for that at bat. It was a situation you thrive on, but I didn't have any butterflies.

02:44:40.290 --> 02:44:45.770
I was really having my great concentration. On Saturday night, after you made the second

02:44:45.770 --> 02:44:50.070
out and you're down by two runs in the bottom of the 10th, you went into Davey Johnson's

02:44:50.070 --> 02:44:51.430
office. Tell us what happened then.

02:44:51.900 --> 02:45:00.000
Well, I went into Davey's office. I figured it was the last at bat of my season. Our season. I grabbed a

02:45:00.000 --> 02:45:06.130
I grabbed a Budweiser, Augie Bush will love that, and drank a Bud and sat in Davey's director's

02:45:06.130 --> 02:45:10.460
chair, and we got two hits, and then the third hit, and got a run in, and all of a sudden

02:45:10.460 --> 02:45:15.010
the timing runs on base, I ran in my locker and got my glove, and then I said, I was going

02:45:15.010 --> 02:45:17.870
halfway out the door and go on the field, and I said, no, that chair's got hits in it,

02:45:17.870 --> 02:45:20.370
and I stayed right there, and that was a remarkable comeback.

02:45:21.180 --> 02:45:22.960
Congratulations for being part of a world champion.

02:45:23.020 --> 02:45:30.000
I promised my three daughters I would say hello, Jessie, Melissa, and Mary Elise, and

02:45:30.000 --> 02:45:32.890
My sister-in-law, Mary Horn, they're behind us all the way.

02:45:32.950 --> 02:45:33.390
I love them.

02:45:33.850 --> 02:45:34.690
I'll see them in a week.

02:45:36.060 --> 02:45:40.790
And from the champagne shampoo, we go back upstairs to Vin Scully.

02:45:40.870 --> 02:45:45.910
And meanwhile, down on the mound with Kevin Elster on his feet and other members of the Mets,

02:45:46.250 --> 02:45:51.370
it has evidently been a ritual when the Mets clinched the division, clinched the pennant,

02:45:51.630 --> 02:45:53.770
why they sat on the mound, several of them.

02:45:54.090 --> 02:45:57.920
And tonight, there are those who remembered Rick Aguilera.

02:45:58.690 --> 02:46:00.000
And then of course we can see

02:46:00.670 --> 02:46:06.820
Howard Johnson and Kevin Elster is there and there is Ron Darling and they

02:46:06.820 --> 02:46:10.540
walked out with large bottles of champagne and of course it's not for

02:46:10.540 --> 02:46:14.910
drinking I think they spill much more than they ever thought of drinking and

02:46:14.910 --> 02:46:21.120
now the crowd salutes them as they can say truly we are number one
